    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Miguel Vargas** serving as our anchor, posting a robust 63.96 rating. His matchup against Andrew Abbott is highly favorable; Abbott\u2019s high xERA (5.02) combined with the third-spot lineup protection provides **Miguel Vargas** with a massive ceiling for run production and base-clearing opportunities. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.31) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.18) provide strong core output, the primary driver for our top-tier scores today is the exploitation of vulnerable left-handed pitching. **Andy Pages** receives a boost in efficiency batting second, and despite the sub-optimal lineup placement for **Kyle Tucker** (7th) and **Sam Antonacci** (8th), their individual profiles against Shane Drohan and Abbott respectively keep them comfortably above the marginal threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning was keeping **Wade Meckler** on the bench with a 38.70 score. While his projected leadoff spot provided a significant boost to his base projection, the presence of Jacob deGrom on the mound\u2014even in a late-career stage\u2014squeezes his efficiency enough to keep him below our active floor. We are prioritizing the higher run-scoring environment afforded to our starting infielders over **Wade Meckler**'s potential speed contribution today. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the statuses of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, both of whom are sidelined today, and we remain cautious regarding **Jordan Westburg**, who remains out due to his current IL stint. Given the scarcity of stolen bases in this league, the benching of **Wade Meckler** is a calculated risk, but we are prioritizing the superior raw point expectation of our starting six to maximize our daily Roto standing.",
